{
 "summary": "Findings: Four actionable issues: unnecessary strategy layers, duplicated channel definitions, an unenforced nonempty-order contract, and missing behavioral tests.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Remove the single-implementation strategy hierarchy",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "delivery.ts:14-20,36-38; alerts.ts:12-18",
   "Failure": "Premature Abstraction: DeliveryStrategy has one implementation, and createDeliveryStrategy unconditionally constructs it. AlertDispatcher creates that implementation internally, so the interface does not even provide caller-selectable behavior. The factory, interface, and class add layers without adding a capability required by ordered fallback.",
   "Fix": "Expose a delivery function that accepts the sender, contact, ordered channels, and text. Call it directly from AlertDispatcher and retain the result types."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Use the existing canonical channel list",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "preferences.ts:3,20",
   "Failure": "Single Source of Truth: ALLOWED_CHANNELS duplicates channels.ts:1 instead of using CHANNELS. The Channel annotation checks individual entries but does not require an exhaustive list. Adding a channel to the canonical definition can therefore leave settings rejecting a supported channel.",
   "Fix": "Import CHANNELS from channels.ts and use it for parser validation. Remove ALLOWED_CHANNELS."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Enforce the nonempty order at the preference boundary",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "preferences.ts:8-9",
   "Failure": "The new field promises a nonempty list but accepts [] as a valid typed value. PreferenceStore.set stores it without validation. A direct store caller can therefore configure zero attempts, unlike the previous required channel field. A runtime probe confirmed that dispatchForFeed then returns 'm: NOT DELIVERED to u; tried ' without calling Sender.send at all. The settings parser enforces the invariant only for its own callers.",
   "Fix": "Enforce the nonempty contract in PreferenceStore.set and represent it in the public preference type, or make the validated settings operation the only supported writer."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Add tests for the new delivery and settings behavior",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "delivery.ts:22-32; preferences.ts:15-25; oncall-feed.ts:4-9",
   "Failure": "The patch introduces ordered retries, error collection, terminal failure results, preference parsing, and feed formatting without any behavioral tests. The complete supplied project contains no test files. Regressions such as continuing after success, reordering attempts, or omitting failed channels from the feed currently have no automated protection.",
   "Fix": "Add focused tests through the public settings, dispatcher, and feed functions. Cover preserving order, stopping at first success, collecting preceding failures, exhaustion, and rejecting empty, unknown, or duplicate settings without overwriting existing preferences."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Read the entire patch and all six project source files. Confirmed all strategy and channel-list references. Ran a Bun probe against the actual preference store, dispatcher, and feed to verify the empty-order behavior. No project files were changed."
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: two P2 issues. The FeatureGate adds indirection without a new contract, and express-shipping behavior has no regression tests. Fresh runtime checks passed; no functional regression was reproduced.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Replace the concrete pass-through gate with a meaningful boundary",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "feature-gate.ts:5-9",
   "failure": "Shallow Wrapper: FeatureGate repeats FlagStore.isEnabled with identical arguments and return semantics. Both pages now depend on another concrete class, while flag names and evaluation policy remain unchanged. The private FlagStore member also ties the page-facing type to this implementation. The claimed delivery independence is not achieved by the added layer.",
   "fix": "Remove the forwarding class and retain direct FlagStore calls, including the new express-shipping check. If delivery independence is required, define a structural page-facing contract and have the provider implement it instead of making the concrete wrapper the contract."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add regression coverage for the new express-shipping option",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "checkout-page.ts:8-11",
   "failure": "The supplied project contains no tests for the added checkout option. A wrong flag key, coupling expressShipping to oneClick, or ignoring rollout eligibility would therefore have no automated regression check.",
   "fix": "Add checkoutOptions tests using the real FlagStore and FeatureGate. Verify independently enabled checkout flags and express-shipping missing, disabled, and rollout-ineligible cases."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "A fresh Bun probe against the actual modules passed for missing flags, independently controlled checkout flags, 0% and 100% rollout, search selection, and rule reloads through an existing gate. No project-wide gate was requested or run.",
 "intent_classification": "The implementation matches the stated checkout/search routing and express-shipping addition. No intent drift was established."
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: Six actionable issues. Basic grouping, duplicate skipping, per-currency reporting, and rejection before posting worked in direct Bun probes. No files were changed.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Reject monetary values that cannot be represented exactly before posting",
   "severity": "P1",
   "location": "src/import/invoice-rows.ts:84-95; src/totals.ts:7,16",
   "failure": "The import accepts numeric text that Number rounds, and createInvoice only checks Number.isInteger. A real import of quantity 9007199254740993 stored 9007199254740992. A unit_price of 90071992547409.93 stored 9007199254740992 cents and displayed USD 90071992547409.92. Two 200-digit quantity/price fields passed validation, posted an invoice, and displayed USD Infinity because multiplication overflowed. Thus whole-file validation permits corrupted ledger amounts.",
   "fix": "Reject quantities and converted cents outside the exact integer range. Validate line products, invoice sums, and per-currency sums before posting anything. Keep formatting exact within the supported amount range."
  },
  {
   "title": "Remove the single-use Pipeline framework",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "src/import/pipeline.ts:3-16; src/import/importer.ts:17,24",
   "failure": "Premature Abstraction: Pipeline has one consumer, one synchronous execution path, and no capability beyond ordinary typed function calls. The compiler already checks the arguments and results of nested or sequential calls. This adds a generic class, nested closures, a module, and a custom execution API without hiding domain complexity.",
   "fix": "Call parseCsv, dataRows, parseInvoiceRows, and groupIntoInvoices directly in order, and delete Pipeline."
  },
  {
   "title": "Do not silently discard invoice lines in the shared total calculation",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "src/totals.ts:6",
   "failure": "Speculative Code: The new skip branch compensates for nonpositive quantities and negative prices, although src/invoice.ts:3-16 identifies createInvoice as the required producer and rejects both conditions. The importer calls that producer at src/import/group.ts:27. No supported producer in the supplied project establishes a need for this fallback, and no evidence for changing the shared total semantics is disclosed. The branch obscures the factory invariant and would conceal invalid data as a plausible partial total.",
   "fix": "Remove the skip condition and retain unconditional summation. Keep payable validation in createInvoice."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add behavioral tests for the import contract",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "src/import/importer.ts:23-33",
   "failure": "The supplied project contains no test files, and the patch adds no tests for this feature. Whole-file rejection without ledger changes, multirow grouping, conflicting invoice metadata, duplicate skipping, and per-currency totals consequently have no regression coverage. Direct probes verified the principal success path and atomic rejection, but they are not retained tests.",
   "fix": "Add tests through importInvoices with a real PayablesLedger, covering these observable contracts and the numeric rejection defect. Assert that a later invalid row leaves the ledger unchanged."
  },
  {
   "title": "Avoid a quadratic scan when identifying skipped invoices",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "src/import/importer.ts:29-30",
   "failure": "Every invoice searches fresh using Array.includes. In an all-new file of n invoices, this performs approximately n(n+1)/2 reference comparisons even though ledger membership was already checked in a linear pass. This is a reachable path for ordinary imports, not duplicate-heavy input. Fresh probes completed 10,000, 20,000, and 40,000 invoice imports in approximately 43, 64, and 159 ms respectively; the source establishes the quadratic scan independently of these timings.",
   "fix": "Partition invoices into fresh invoices and alreadyPosted identifiers using ledger.has in one pass. Do not recover the skipped partition through repeated array searches."
  },
  {
   "title": "Report the actual row containing an invalid invoice line",
   "severity": "P3",
   "location": "src/import/group.ts:34-35",
   "failure": "All createInvoice errors are attributed to the invoice's first row, even when a later line fails validation. A probe with a valid line on CSV row 2 and quantity 0 on row 3 returned 'Row 2: Invoice i: quantity of \"bad\" must be a whole number of at least 1'. The clerk is directed to the wrong row.",
   "fix": "Preserve each line's source row through validation and map line validation errors to that row. Keep createInvoice as the authoritative payable-rule validator rather than duplicating its rules."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Executed direct Bun 1.4.4 probes against the supplied modules. Verified grouping, currency totals, repeat-import skipping, unchanged ledger after a later invalid invoice, unsafe numeric acceptance, overflow reporting, and incorrect row attribution. No suite-level gate was run because none was assigned and no test configuration exists in the supplied tree."
}

{
 "summary": "Found one shipping regression caused by duplicated payment state, one incorrect payment classification, and missing behavioral tests. Runtime probes reproduced both behavioral defects.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Derive payment status instead of caching it on mutable orders",
   "severity": "P1",
   "location": "orders.ts:25-29; orders.ts:42; fulfillment.ts:5; account-page.ts:15",
   "failure": "Single Source of Truth: paymentStatus duplicates information in lines and payments, but refreshes only in open() and recordPayment(). open() retains the caller's line objects, and open() and forCustomer() expose mutable orders and payment arrays. A runtime probe paid a $10 order, then changed the retained line's quantity to two. balanceDueCents() returned 1000, but readyToShip() returned true and the account displayed 'Paid in full  ($10.00 due)'. Another probe appended a full payment through the public payments array: the balance became zero, but shipping remained blocked and the account displayed 'Awaiting payment'. Previously shipping derived its answer from the current balance.",
   "fix": "Keep lines and payments as the canonical data. Expose paymentStatus as a derived, read-only getter using paymentStatusOf(), and remove its manual assignments. Account display and shipping can then consume the same current derived status."
  },
  {
   "title": "Classify payment status by the amount received, not the number of records",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "orders.ts:14-16",
   "failure": "recordPayment() accepts a zero-amount payment because its only validation rejects overpayment. A runtime probe recorded zero cents against a $10 order. paymentStatusOf() returned 'partially-paid' and the account displayed 'Partially paid', although no money had been received. A nonempty payments array does not establish partial payment.",
   "fix": "Derive the unpaid versus partially-paid distinction from the net payment amount rather than payments.length, while retaining the fully settled balance check."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add behavioral coverage for the new payment-status contract",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "orders.ts:14-16; fulfillment.ts:4-5; account-page.ts:11-15",
   "failure": "Neither the supplied project nor diff.patch contains tests. The new three-state classification, account rendering, and status-based shipping decision therefore have no regression coverage, including the reproduced stale-state and zero-payment failures.",
   "fix": "Add tests against the production OrderBook, orderLines(), and readyToShip() functions. Cover unpaid, partial, and full payments, zero-value payments, and mutation through the public references that must not leave status stale."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "A Bun runtime probe imported the supplied production modules and reproduced stale paid status after retained-line mutation, stale unpaid status after public payment-array mutation, and partial status after a zero-cent payment. No files were changed."
}

{
 "summary": "Found five actionable issues: a domain/UI dependency cycle, duplicated ownership of column membership, ignored command arguments, lossy integer parsing, and missing regression tests. Core ordering, WIP rejection, blocker-age preservation, and rendering passed a direct Bun probe.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Move the WIP rule out of the rendering layer",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "src/domain/board.ts:1",
   "Failure": "Bidirectional Coupling: domain/board imports exceedsWipLimit from ui/board-view, which imports cardsIn from domain/board. This creates a runtime dependency cycle and violates ARCHITECTURE.md:3-5: domain must not depend on UI, and board rules belong in domain. Every domain consumer now loads terminal rendering modules merely to enforce capacity.",
   "Fix": "Define and export exceedsWipLimit in the domain layer. Import that domain rule from board-view, keeping dependencies one-way."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Keep column membership in one authoritative representation",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "src/domain/board.ts:55-58; src/domain/types.ts:7,18",
   "Failure": "Parallel State: column membership now exists both in Column.cardIds and Card.columnId. addCard writes both representations, and moveCard manually synchronizes them. WIP enforcement and rendering read cardIds, while moveCard locates the source through columnId. This gives the same relationship two owners and makes agreement a permanent mutation invariant. No divergence occurred in the inspected domain operations; the finding is structural debt, not a demonstrated corruption claim.",
   "Fix": "Store membership once and derive the other view. For example, retain Card.columnId and derive column contents from a canonically ordered board.cards collection."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Reject extra arguments to fixed-arity commands",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "src/ui/commands.ts:30-33,40-48",
   "Failure": "move, unblock, and limit check only missing arguments and silently discard trailing tokens. A Bun probe confirmed that commands ending in EXTRA are accepted and applied. For example, `limit col_2 2 EXTRA` changes the limit instead of rejecting malformed syntax. This contradicts the parser's syntax-validation contract and hides terminal input mistakes.",
   "Fix": "Require exactly three arguments for move, one for unblock, and two for limit. Keep variable-length arguments for add and block."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Reject integers that cannot be represented exactly",
   "Severity": "P3",
   "Location": "src/ui/commands.ts:75-78",
   "Failure": "Number converts the token before Number.isInteger checks it. The probe confirmed that `limit col_2 9007199254740993` parses as 9007199254740992, so the command silently substitutes a different integer. checkedWipLimit also accepts that rounded value.",
   "Fix": "Use Number.isSafeInteger for parsed numeric arguments and domain WIP limits, rejecting unsupported magnitudes instead of rounding them."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Add regression coverage for the new board rules and parser",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "src/domain/board.ts:33-98; src/ui/commands.ts:22-78",
   "Failure": "The complete supplied tree and patch contain no tests for the added behavior. No automated regression protects capacity rejection without mutation, same-column ordering at capacity, positional moves, retained blocker start times, or parser validation. These are observable contracts introduced by this change.",
   "Fix": "Add focused behavioral tests covering those contracts, including malformed command arity and unrepresentable integers. Exercise the production domain functions and parser rather than copies of their logic."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Ran one direct Bun probe against the supplied implementation. It verified same-column reordering, cross-column WIP rejection, preservation of the original blocked timestamp after changing the reason, and rendered blocked age. It also reproduced acceptance and execution of trailing command arguments and loss of integer precision. Read every supplied source file, the complete diff, and ARCHITECTURE.md. No project-wide gate was run."
}

{
 "summary": "Findings: Two P2 issues: the settings path ignores XDG_CONFIG_HOME, and the new settings behavior has no committed regression tests. Runtime probes confirmed correct loading from ~/.config, but settings in a custom config directory were silently ignored.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Honor the user's configured configuration directory",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "main.ts:7",
   "failure": "SETTINGS_PATH always uses ~/.config. With HOME pointing to an empty home and XDG_CONFIG_HOME pointing to a directory containing deskcal/settings.json with Sunday and Asia/Tokyo settings, invoking main() printed Monday-first headings and 00:00 at epoch zero. The same file under ~/.config produced Sunday-first headings and 09:00. Users who relocate their config directory therefore silently receive defaults instead of their preferences. XDG_CONFIG_HOME defines the user configuration directory; ~/.config is its fallback, not its unconditional value. Source: https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir/latest/",
   "fix": "Resolve the configuration base from a nonempty, absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME, otherwise use join(homedir(), '.config'), then append deskcal/settings.json."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add regression coverage for settings loading and validation",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "settings-file.ts:7-29; main.ts:10-13",
   "failure": "The diff adds file discovery, partial-default merging, strict JSON validation, and settings propagation without any automated tests. The complete supplied project contains no tests. Reverting main() to use DEFAULT_SETTINGS, dropping one field assignment, or rejecting an omitted field would therefore have no regression check.",
   "fix": "Add parser tests for missing and partial settings, both valid fields, and invalid input. Add an isolated main() integration test using temporary HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME directories, a fixed clock, and assertions for the printed headings and time."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Ran a Bun probe against the actual main() in isolated subprocesses with temporary configuration directories and a fixed timestamp. Also exercised the actual parser and calendar functions with absent settings, an empty object, valid overrides, invalid week start, invalid time zone, an unknown key, null, and malformed JSON. No project-wide gate was run."
}

{
 "summary": "Found three actionable issues: unnecessary delivery-strategy indirection, duplicated channel definitions, and missing behavioral tests. Runtime probes passed for the implemented settings, fallback, and feed behavior.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Remove the single-implementation strategy interface and factory",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "delivery.ts:14-16,36-38; alerts.ts:12-18",
   "Failure": "Depth over Indirection: AlertDispatcher always obtains FallbackDeliveryStrategy through createDeliveryStrategy. The interface has one implementation, and the factory has one caller and makes no selection. These layers add ownership and navigation without adding substitution or delivery capability.",
   "Fix": "Keep the delivery module, but instantiate its concrete delivery class directly. Remove the redundant strategy interface and factory."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Use the canonical channel list for settings validation",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "preferences.ts:3,20",
   "Failure": "Single Source of Truth: ALLOWED_CHANNELS repeats the complete channel list already exported as CHANNELS in channels.ts:1. The Channel annotation rejects invalid additions but does not require completeness. Channel definitions and settings validation can therefore diverge, requiring synchronized maintenance.",
   "Fix": "Import CHANNELS from channels.ts and use it for the parser lookup. Delete ALLOWED_CHANNELS."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Add behavioral coverage for the new settings-to-feed path",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "delivery.ts:22-32; preferences.ts:15-25; oncall-feed.ts:4-9",
   "Failure": "The patch adds no tests, and the supplied project contains none. Its defining contracts are therefore unprotected: ordered attempts, stopping after success, collecting failures, reporting total failure, and rejecting invalid settings without replacing saved preferences.",
   "Fix": "Add focused tests using a recording Sender at the existing injection boundary. Cover ordered fallback and early termination, first-attempt success, complete failure reporting, and invalid settings preserving prior preferences."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "A fresh Bun assertion probe passed for saved order, channel-specific addresses, unchanged alert text, fallback order, early stopping, duplicate/unknown/empty input rejection, first-attempt success, and all-channel failure feed output. No runtime behavior defect was observed in those cases. No project-wide gate was run."
}

{
 "summary": "Found six actionable issues: stale credentials after sign-out, refresh sharing across different sessions, duplicate refreshes for delayed 401s, incorrect sign-out on token-endpoint errors, missing regression tests, and an unreachable expiry fallback.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Read the access token from the session instead of maintaining a client-side copy",
   "severity": "P1",
   "location": "session-store.ts:21-23; api-client.ts:14,39-42",
   "failure": "Single Source of Truth: attach() retains only the latest ApiClient, but earlier clients remain usable. After constructing two clients with one signed-in store and calling signOut(), the first client still sends the old bearer token. A Bun probe reproduced this exact request. The new bidirectional store/client coupling therefore breaks sign-out credential removal and also leaves older clients stale after sign-in or refresh.",
   "fix": "Read store.get()?.tokens.accessToken in send(), as before. Remove the cached token, setter, attach(), and store-to-client notifications."
  },
  {
   "title": "Scope refresh sharing to the session being refreshed",
   "severity": "P1",
   "location": "api-client.ts:32,46-50",
   "failure": "The refreshing promise belongs to the client, not a session. If session A starts refreshing, then signIn() installs expiring session B, B's get() joins A's refresh. replaceTokens() correctly discards A's result, but B's request then proceeds without refreshing B. A controlled transport probe produced one refresh POST, two requests using B's original token, and a store that remained expiring. An old session's rejected refresh would also reject B's waiting request.",
   "fix": "Associate refresh work with its originating session. A caller for a replacement session must refresh that session rather than accept the previous session's completion. Preserve the existing identity check when installing results."
  },
  {
   "title": "Do not refresh again for a delayed 401 from an already-replaced token",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "api-client.ts:33-36",
   "failure": "Two concurrent requests can use the same token, but receive their 401s at different times. If the first request finishes refreshing before the second 401 arrives, refreshing has already been cleared. The second request then performs another exchange even though its failed token has already been replaced. A deferred-response probe reproduced two refresh POSTs for two overlapping GETs using the same original token.",
   "fix": "Track the session/token used for each request. If that token has already been refreshed within the same session, use the available replacement for the single retry instead of exchanging again."
  },
  {
   "title": "Check the OAuth error before discarding the session",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "api-client.ts:62-64",
   "failure": "The comment describes invalid_grant, but the condition signs out on every 400 or 401. OAuth also uses these statuses for invalid_request and invalid_client, which do not establish that the user's refresh token is revoked. A transport probe returning HTTP 400 with error=invalid_request cleared the session. The status distinctions are documented at https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6749.html#section-5.2. No live endpoint was supplied, so the actual server's error responses were not verified.",
   "fix": "Validate the token-endpoint error body and sign out only for the error that establishes an unusable refresh token, while retaining the session-identity check. Propagate other failures without deleting the session."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add behavioral tests for the refresh lifecycle",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "api-client.ts:31-69; session-store.ts:30-52",
   "failure": "The patch adds expiry refresh, retry, shared asynchronous state, and session replacement behavior without any tests. The supplied project contains no test files. Consequently, neither the requested behavior nor the reproduced concurrency and sign-out regressions have automated coverage.",
   "fix": "Add tests exercising the real ApiClient and SessionStore with a controlled HttpTransport and clock. Cover pre-request refresh, exactly one 401 retry, concurrent refresh sharing, and sign-out/sign-in during refresh."
  },
  {
   "title": "Remove the unreachable expiry fallback",
   "severity": "P3",
   "location": "api-client.ts:65-69; api-client.ts:5",
   "failure": "parseTokenPair() throws unless expiresIn is finite and strictly positive, as defined in tokens.ts:16-18. Therefore pair.expiresIn > 0 is always true here. DEFAULT_EXPIRES_IN_SECONDS and the fallback branch cannot affect behavior and misleadingly suggest that invalid lifetimes receive a default.",
   "fix": "Pass the validated pair directly to replaceTokens() and remove DEFAULT_EXPIRES_IN_SECONDS."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Read the complete patch and all six project files. Ran one Bun command against the production ApiClient and SessionStore with deterministic transport responses; reproduced stale bearer credentials after sign-out, two refresh exchanges for delayed concurrent 401s, cross-session refresh sharing, and session deletion on invalid_request. No project files were changed."
}

{
 "summary": "Found three actionable defects. The formatter extraction preserves the sampled CSV and summary behavior, but the new export can emit records longer than its documented 36-character layout.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Reject values that exceed the fixed-width fields",
   "severity": "P1",
   "location": "export.ts:17",
   "failure": "The exporter concatenates formatted values without enforcing the documented field widths. With account \"123456789012\", amountCents 10000000000000 produces a 37-character record: the 14-character amount field reads \"100000000000.0\", losing the final decimal digit. A valid timestamp from Date.UTC(10000, 0, 1) also produces 37 characters and shifts the account and amount offsets. Both inputs satisfy Transaction's documented constraints. Direct execution confirmed both failures.",
   "fix": "Validate that the formatted date occupies exactly 10 characters and the amount fits 14 characters before emitting a record. Reject unrepresentable values explicitly instead of truncating financial data."
  },
  {
   "title": "Add behavioral coverage for the new record format",
   "severity": "P2",
   "location": "export.ts:15-18",
   "failure": "The supplied project and diff contain no tests for the new export. Its externally consumed field offsets and record lengths therefore have no regression coverage; direct execution already exposes malformed records.",
   "fix": "Add tests against renderFixedWidth that assert exact records and field offsets, including ordinary signed amounts, multiple records, and explicit rejection of field overflow."
  },
  {
   "title": "Replace the custom padding implementation with the runtime primitive",
   "severity": "P3",
   "location": "export.ts:21-24",
   "failure": "Depth over Indirection: padLeft duplicates String.prototype.padStart and exposes a configurable fill argument despite having only one caller, which always supplies a space. It adds an implementation to maintain without adding behavior. A runtime probe confirmed padStart produces the required amount padding.",
   "fix": "Call formatAmount(tx.amountCents).padStart(AMOUNT_WIDTH, \" \") directly and delete padLeft. Keep the separate field-overflow validation, since padStart does not enforce a maximum width."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "Executed the actual exports with Bun. Confirmed an ordinary record is 36 characters, amount overflow and a five-digit year each produce 37 characters, and the sampled CSV and summary outputs remain correct. No project-wide gates were run."
}

{
 "summary": "Found two review issues: missing pagination regression tests (P2) and an unsupported defensive cursor-cycle policy (P3). The supplied implementation passed a direct two-page check for both list functions, including an empty intermediate page and cursor encoding. No functional pagination failure was demonstrated.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "Title": "Add behavioral coverage for pagination",
   "Severity": "P2",
   "Location": "pagination.ts:16-22",
   "Failure": "The change adds no tests, and the supplied project contains none. No regression test protects continuation requests, aggregation across pages, or cursor encoding. Returning only the first page would therefore break the required behavior without failing any project test.",
   "Fix": "Add tests through listProjects and listMembers that return multiple pages and assert complete results and continuation paths. Include an empty page with a non-null cursor and a cursor requiring encoding."
  },
  {
   "Title": "Remove or substantiate the cursor-cycle policy",
   "Severity": "P3",
   "Location": "pagination.ts:13,19-21",
   "Failure": "Speculative Code: the helper introduces cursor-history state and a new rejection policy for repeated cursor strings. Neither the supplied service contract nor a producer establishes that repeated strings can occur or necessarily mean a cycle. The comment asserts this risk without supporting evidence, contrary to the required elegance lens.",
   "Fix": "Remove the cursor-history set and rejection branch unless service evidence establishes this failure mode. If established, document the contract and test the observed case."
  }
 ],
 "verification": "A fresh Bun invocation exercised the actual exported list functions against controlled page responses. Both lists fetched their second page, preserved results, encoded the organization and opaque cursor, and followed an empty page with a non-null cursor. No live service endpoint or implementation was supplied, so actual service response semantics remain unverified."
}

{
 "summary": "Found six actionable issues. Grouping, per-currency totals, and skipping posted invoices worked for ordinary inputs. Runtime probes reproduced monetary corruption and incorrect error-row attribution. No files were changed.",
 "files_modified": [],
 "findings": [
  {
   "title": "Reject amounts and totals that cannot be represented exactly",
   "severity": "P1",
